---
<BaseLayout title="Protocol">
<section class="hero" style="height:700px"><img src="/images/untangling-mental-strongholds.jpg" srcset="/images/untangling-mental-strongholds-1200.jpg 1200w, /images/untangling-mental-strongholds.jpg 2576w" sizes="100vw" alt="Untangling Mental Strongholds" style="object-position:center 50%;filter:brightness(.5)" fetchpriority="high" /><div class="veil"></div><SiteNav />
<div class="hero-c" style="top:252px;padding:0 24px"><span class="eb">The Perimeter · Protocol III</span><h1 class="h1" style="margin-top:22px">Untangling Mental Strongholds</h1><p class="it" style="margin:24px 0 0;max-width:680px;font-size:26px;line-height:1.4;color:#E6DFD0">A recovery manual, step by step.</p></div></section>
<section class="sec paper"><div class="side"><aside class="rv" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:18px;align-self:start;position:sticky;top:110px">
<span class="eb">In this protocol</span><span class="lab" style="padding:12px 0;border-top:1px solid rgba(42,32,23,.2)">Step 1 · Name the stronghold</span><span class="lab" style="padding:12px 0;border-top:1px solid rgba(42,32,23,.2)">Step 2 · Bring it into the light</span><span class="lab" style="padding:12px 0;border-top:1px solid rgba(42,32,23,.2)">Step 3 · Renounce and replace</span><span class="lab" style="padding:12px 0;border-top:1px solid rgba(42,32,23,.2)">Step 4 · Establish the new boundary</span><span class="lab" style="padding:12px 0;border-top:1px solid rgba(42,32,23,.2)">Step 5 · Keep watch</span>
<button type="button" class="btn" style="margin-top:14px;align-self:flex-start" onclick="window.print()">Print / Download</button>
<p class="it mut" style="margin:6px 0 0;font-size:16px;line-height:1.45">Spiritual and practical guidance, not legal, medical or psychological advice. <a href="/legal" style="border-bottom:1px solid">Read the disclaimer.</a></p></aside>
<div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:30px">
<p class="lede" style="font-size:30px">For anyone who knows the thought that keeps winning: the old accusation, the fear that will not leave, the voice that sounds like your own. This manual walks through five movements for bringing it under the obedience of Christ.</p>
<div class="rv" style="padding:36px;background:#F1ECE2;box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(42,32,23,.15);display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px"><div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:18px"><span class="num" style="color:#62372D;font-size:60px">1</span><span class="h3">Name the stronghold</span></div><p class="body">A stronghold is a lie that has hardened into a way of thinking. Before it can be pulled down, it has to be named plainly and without shame.</p><div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:10px"><label class="lab" style="display:flex;gap:14px;align-items:center;letter-spacing:.14em"><span style="width:16px;height:16px;border:1px solid #2A2017;display:inline-block"></span>Write the recurring thought down, word for word.</label><label class="lab" style="display:flex;gap:14px;align-items:center;letter-spacing:.14em"><span style="width:16px;height:16px;border:1px solid #2A2017;display:inline-block"></span>Note when it speaks loudest: the time, the place, the trigger.</label><label class="lab" style="display:flex;gap:14px;align-items:center;letter-spacing:.14em"><span style="width:16px;height:16px;border:1px solid #2A2017;display:inline-block"></span>Ask what it claims about God, about you, and about others.</label></div><div style="padding:18px 22px;border-left:2px solid #9F945E"><span class="it" style="font-size:20px">Bringing into captivity every thought to the obedience of Christ. · 2 Corinthians x · v</span></div></div><div class="rv" style="padding:36px;background:#F1ECE2;box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(42,32,23,.15);display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px"><div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:18px"><span class="num" style="color:#62372D;font-size:60px">2</span><span class="h3">Bring it into the light</span></div><p class="body">What stays hidden keeps its power. Confession breaks the secrecy a stronghold depends on.</p><div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:10px"><label class="lab" style="display:flex;gap:14px;align-items:center;letter-spacing:.14em"><span style="width:16px;height:16px;border:1px solid #2A2017;display:inline-block"></span>Bring what you have written to God in prayer, out loud.</label><label class="lab" style="display:flex;gap:14px;align-items:center;letter-spacing:.14em"><span style="width:16px;height:16px;border:1px solid #2A2017;display:inline-block"></span>Tell one trusted, mature believer what you have named.</label><label class="lab" style="display:flex;gap:14px;align-items:center;letter-spacing:.14em"><span style="width:16px;height:16px;border:1px solid #2A2017;display:inline-block"></span>Let them pray with you, and receive it.</label></div><div style="padding:18px 22px;border-left:2px solid #9F945E"><span class="it" style="font-size:20px">If we walk in the light, as he is in the light, we have fellowship one with another. · 1 John i · vii</span></div></div><div class="rv" style="padding:36px;background:#F1ECE2;box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(42,32,23,.15);display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px"><div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:18px"><span class="num" style="color:#62372D;font-size:60px">3</span><span class="h3">Renounce and replace</span></div><p class="body">A lie is not only refused; it is replaced. Answer it with what God has actually said.</p><div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:10px"><label class="lab" style="display:flex;gap:14px;align-items:center;letter-spacing:.14em"><span style="width:16px;height:16px;border:1px solid #2A2017;display:inline-block"></span>Renounce the lie by name, in the authority of Christ.</label><label class="lab" style="display:flex;gap:14px;align-items:center;letter-spacing:.14em"><span style="width:16px;height:16px;border:1px solid #2A2017;display:inline-block"></span>Find the passage of Scripture that answers it directly.</label><label class="lab" style="display:flex;gap:14px;align-items:center;letter-spacing:.14em"><span style="width:16px;height:16px;border:1px solid #2A2017;display:inline-block"></span>Write that truth where the old thought used to win.</label></div><div style="padding:18px 22px;border-left:2px solid #9F945E"><span class="it" style="font-size:20px">And ye shall know the truth, and the truth shall make you free. · John viii · xxxii</span></div></div><div class="rv" style="padding:36px;background:#F1ECE2;box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(42,32,23,.15);display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px"><div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:18px"><span class="num" style="color:#62372D;font-size:60px">4</span><span class="h3">Establish the new boundary</span></div><p class="body">Freedom has to be guarded. Decide in advance what you will no longer let in.</p><div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:10px"><label class="lab" style="display:flex;gap:14px;align-items:center;letter-spacing:.14em"><span style="width:16px;height:16px;border:1px solid #2A2017;display:inline-block"></span>Identify the voices, habits and places that fed the lie.</label><label class="lab" style="display:flex;gap:14px;align-items:center;letter-spacing:.14em"><span style="width:16px;height:16px;border:1px solid #2A2017;display:inline-block"></span>Choose one concrete limit for each, and tell someone.</label><label class="lab" style="display:flex;gap:14px;align-items:center;letter-spacing:.14em"><span style="width:16px;height:16px;border:1px solid #2A2017;display:inline-block"></span>Plan what you will do instead when the old pull returns.</label></div><div style="padding:18px 22px;border-left:2px solid #9F945E"><span class="it" style="font-size:20px">Keep thy heart with all diligence; for out of it are the issues of life. · Proverbs iv · xxiii</span></div></div><div class="rv" style="padding:36px;background:#F1ECE2;box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(42,32,23,.15);display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px"><div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:18px"><span class="num" style="color:#62372D;font-size:60px">5</span><span class="h3">Keep watch</span></div><p class="body">Strongholds rarely fall in a day. Walls are rebuilt the same way they were taken: one stone at a time, under watch.</p><div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:10px"><label class="lab" style="display:flex;gap:14px;align-items:center;letter-spacing:.14em"><span style="width:16px;height:16px;border:1px solid #2A2017;display:inline-block"></span>Return to your written truth every morning for forty days.</label><label class="lab" style="display:flex;gap:14px;align-items:center;letter-spacing:.14em"><span style="width:16px;height:16px;border:1px solid #2A2017;display:inline-block"></span>Keep a short record of each victory, however small.</label><label class="lab" style="display:flex;gap:14px;align-items:center;letter-spacing:.14em"><span style="width:16px;height:16px;border:1px solid #2A2017;display:inline-block"></span>If the battle exceeds you, seek pastoral and professional help without shame.</label></div><div style="padding:18px 22px;border-left:2px solid #9F945E"><span class="it" style="font-size:20px">Be sober, be vigilant. · 1 Peter v · viii</span></div></div>
